82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 53 0 R
/T (The College Student Management System is a simple menu-driven Java application made to manage basic student details. It allows the user to add, display, search, sort, update and delete student records. Each record contains a roll number, student name, course and marks. The main purpose of this project is to practise the Java concepts taught in college, especially ArrayList, searching, sorting and HashMap. An ArrayList is used to keep student objects because its size can change while the program is running. Linear search is used to find a student by roll number or name. Collections.sort\(\) with Comparator is used to sort records by name or marks. A HashMap keeps a course-wise count of students. The program takes input through the Scanner class and shows results in the console.)
/E (The College Student Management System is a simple menu-driven Java application made to manage basic student details. It allows the user to add, display, search, sort, update and delete student records. Each record contains a roll number, student name, course and marks. The main purpose of this project is to practise the Java concepts taught in college, especially ArrayList, searching, sorting and HashMap. An ArrayList is used to keep student objects because its size can change while the program is running. Linear search is used to find a student by roll number or name. Collections.sort\(\) with Comparator is used to sort records by name or marks. A HashMap keeps a course-wise count of students. The program takes input through the Scanner class and shows results in the console.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
