>>
endobj
609 0 obj
<<
/Title (Colleges need to maintain information about students, such as their roll numbers, names, courses and marks. If these details are handled manually, searching for a particular student or arranging records can take extra time. This project shows how a small Java program can make these basic tasks easier. When the program starts, it displays a menu. The user selects an option by entering its number. For example, the user can choose Add Student to enter a new record, Search Student to find a record, or Sort Students to arrange the list. The program continues showing the menu until the user selects Exit. The project is divided into two main parts: the Student class, which represents one student, and the CollegeStudentManagementSystem class, which contains the menu and operations.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 462 0 R
>>
endobj
